WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.433
Stress is a normal response to demand, uncertainty, and consequence.

00:00:04.433 --> 00:00:08.475
Some pressure can sharpen attention and create useful urgency.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:15.777
Too much pressure can narrow thinking, reduce patience, increase impulsive action, and make communication worse.

00:00:15.777 --> 00:00:22.361
Human performance improves when teams can tell the difference between useful activation and overload.

00:00:22.361 --> 00:00:25.881
Arousal and performance have a practical relationship.

00:00:25.881 --> 00:00:29.337
Very low activation can feel unfocused or disengaged.

00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:32.792
Moderate activation can support readiness and effort.

00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:37.095
Excessive activation can interfere with judgment and coordination.

00:00:37.095 --> 00:00:39.507
The point is not to eliminate stress.

00:00:39.507 --> 00:00:45.570
The point is to manage pressure so people can still think, communicate, and act deliberately.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:51.437
Emotional regulation is the ability to notice internal state and choose a useful response.

00:00:51.437 --> 00:01:00.825
Simple pause techniques, slow breathing, naming the next action, and asking for a short reset can help create space between stimulus and action.

00:01:00.825 --> 00:01:08.322
These are practical work techniques, not substitutes for qualified care when health or safety concerns are present.

00:01:08.322 --> 00:01:10.734
Preparation reduces avoidable stress.

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:15.949
Pre-briefs clarify goals, roles, risks, and escalation paths before work begins.

00:01:15.949 --> 00:01:18.688
Debriefs help teams learn after the event.

00:01:18.688 --> 00:01:25.207
Good systems reduce uncertainty by making priorities, responsibilities, and decision rights visible.

00:01:25.207 --> 00:01:30.031
Under pressure, people should not have to invent the process from scratch.

00:01:30.031 --> 00:01:33.682
A practical habit is to name the next controllable step.

00:01:33.682 --> 00:01:38.571
Under pressure, people can become trapped in the size of the whole problem.

00:01:38.571 --> 00:01:44.243
A clear next action narrows attention without denying the seriousness of the situation.

00:01:44.243 --> 00:01:49.980
This helps individuals and teams move from emotional reaction toward coordinated action.
